---
description: Keep .env in sync when .env.example changes
globs: "**/.env.example"
alwaysApply: true
---

# .env.example ↔ .env sync

When you **add, rename, or change the default** of any variable in a `.env.example` file,
update the matching **`.env`** in the **same directory** in the same change.

## Layout

| `.env.example` | Mirror to |
|---|---|
| `.env.example` (repo root) | `.env` (repo root) |
| `backend/.env.example` | `backend/.env` |
| `frontend/.env.example` | `frontend/.env` |

When a variable is shared across apps, update **both** the component `.env.example` and the
root `.env.example` (if used), then mirror each to its `.env`.

## Rules

- Add missing keys to `.env` with the same placeholder/default as `.env.example`.
- Do not add tunables (pool sizes, page sizes, timeouts, cache TTLs) to `.env.example` —
  those belong in named constants (`env-config.mdc`).
- **Do not overwrite** existing secret values in `.env` — only add the key or update documented
  non-secret defaults when intentionally changing the default.
- **Never commit** `.env` files.
- **Do not read or print** `.env` contents in chat or logs.
